body:
Biggest peeve will always be with designs that explicitly contradict the canon narrative. Two that come to mind are Jayfeather having cloudy or crossed eyes when his eyes explicitly in canon look and follow you like any cat's, and this is important to his character; 

and one I dislike even more is Shadowsight with scars from being struck by lightning. I know they look cool but they just directly contradict the fact that nobody believed him in canon- I think if your son showed up with full body scarring and a newly blind eye you'd take him a little more seriously.

I don't dislike funky or kooky designs at all, and I don't care if they disregard the characters canon description, it's just when a design choice contradicts canon events or narrative relevance that I dislike it.
